

                   ADVENTURER-KINGS:  GAME 3, TURN 5

                                  FOR

                   SHAMAN UGA-BUGA MAKUMBU











  Quote of the Week:

  "The King of England has men, horses, silk, jewels, fruit, game and 
everything else.  And we in France have nothing but bread and wine and 
gaiety!"
  -Louis VII, King of France, 1179 A.D.


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:


  Winter gave way to sweet spring, and Uga-Buga Makumb made ready to carry 
out his imperial assignments.  He informed Kwoth (#3) that our friendship 
has been rendered worthless by Kwoth's outrageous provocations.
  With the coming of the spring season, Uga-Buga Makumb set out to quench 
his thirst for adventure.  Presto cast a Phantasmal Armies spell and 
illusory armies were formed for Uga-Buga Makumb.
  Uga-Buga Makumb flew into the Moonshine Sea.  West of here lies the 
prosperous province of the Flying Fish Sea (#606), ruled by Circe.  It is 
said to be a Sea province inhabited by no races.  To the northwest lies a 
rich Jungle area called Tabora (#705), populated by Humans.  It is ruled by 
Kwoth.  Their Human fighters traditionally array themselves as Legion and 
Elephants.

  Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll's minions initiated a campaign of 
conquest directed at the Moonshine Sea, a Sea province owing allegiance to 
Circe (#8).  Uga-Buga Makumb commanded the attacking fleet.  The defenders 
were led by Duqaq (#50).  The armies were drawn up into lines of battle as 
shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of the Moonshine Sea (0706):

