  DEFENDING ARMY

  The attackers had the 241st Bowmen, the 272nd Dragons, the 109th 
Heavy Cavalry, the 110th Bowmen, the 277th Eagles and the 209th Warg Riders 
in reserve.  Standing tall with my warriors was I.  No generals were present 
to lead the forces of the provincial Whale chieftain.
  The Skeletal Armies led by Uga-Buga Makumb marched into battle with a 
fanatical fervor.  No luck or misfortune of great significance altered the 
engagement.  In this slugging match, I seemed to gain the tactical upper 
hand.

  Across the whole front, the Crack 108th Skeletal Bowmen were inspired to 
fanatiscm by me, their heroic First Elder of Elvenkind.  They faced the 
149th Whales.  The 124th Skeletal Dragons soared over the 149th Whales and 
attacked them.  The 240th Bowmen and the 241st Bowmen flanked the 
undermanned enemy lines and charged in with full force.  The 108th Skeletal 
Bowmen battled the 149th Whales and crushed their skulls as if they were 
eggplants.
  Guerin's great horde overwhelmed the army of the provincial Whale 
chieftain and took the field, scattering their enemies.
  Guerin's campaign effected the conquest of Mercia.  The 149th Whales could 
not retreat and were paroled into the population.
  The hot days of summer mellowed into fall.  I marched on Bronzeleaf 
(#1303) with my forces.  To the northeast there lies a Forest province known 
as Sherwood (#1302), a rich land of Humans where Kahn reigns.  Their Human 
warriors array themselves as Legion and Light Cavalry.  Viewing the 
northwestern horizon, a man can see a Forest province known as Peachwood 
(#1202).  It is said that no one reigns there.  It is known to be occupied 
by Ents.  They can call on an army of Ents to defend their territory.  I 
discovered a previously unknown Cave (#44) in Bronzeleaf, held by 
the Rakshasha.  What treasure may lie there is unknown.  The Rakshasha is a 
strong, evil spirit encased in flesh.  Of Hindu origin, it has great powers 
of illusion.
  Tornadoes sucked up the 272nd Dragons in Bronzeleaf and destroyed them.
  An army sent by the empire of Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll invaded 
Bronzeleaf, hoping to conquer that province owned by the provincial garrison 
commander and made up of great Forests.  I was in command of the attacking 
armies.  The defending forces were led by the provincial garrison commander. 
The armies were drawn up into lines of battle as shown here:

