 147th/A   145th/A   146th/A   148th/A  
  Legion    Legion    Legion    Legion  
                                        
  DEFENDING ARMY

  Standing at the ready with my warriors was I.  No generals were present to 
lead the forces of the acting commander.
  The Skeletal Armies led by Uga-Buga Makumb marched into battle with a 
fanatical fervor.  The opposing armies strived mightily for the high ground, 
and I obtained an advantage by getting there before the enemy.  Also, my 
wise tactical maneuvers assured my forces an undeniable advantage.

  Out on the left outside flank, the Crack 108th Skeletal Bowmen faced the 
147th Legion.  The 209th Warg Riders outflanked the undermanned enemy lines 
and charged in with full strength.  The 108th Skeletal Bowmen battled the 
147th Legion and beat them down as if they were invalids.
  In the interior front, the Veteran 110th Bowmen were arrayed against the 
145th Legion.  In this sector, the 110th Bowmen's commander led his troops 
badly because he had opium-smoked all through that night, not having 
foreseen a battle with the enemy so soon.  Even so, the 110th Bowmen battled 
the 145th Legion and gradually pushed them back.
  Within the interior lines, the Crack 240th Bowmen were arrayed against the 
146th Legion.  The 124th Skeletal Dragons soared over the 146th Legion and 
attacked without mercy.  The 240th Bowmen fought the 146th Legion and 
squashed them like rotten tomatoes.
  Out on the right flank, the Crack 241st Bowmen were arrayed against the 
148th Legion.  The 277th Eagles soared over the 148th Legion and attacked 
them.  On this field, the soldiers of the 241st Bowmen had queasy stomachs 
because of the sickening local food and fell slightly ill.  They entered 
battle at a minor disadvantage.  It seemed that the 148th Legion might break 
through and win.
  But then the tide of battle reversed.  The 148th Legion carelessly 
blundered into a nest of booby traps and lost some of their best 
battle-hardened troops.  The 241st Bowmen battled the 148th Legion and 
thrust them back with a savage fury.
  The battle ended victoriously for the soldiers of Guerin as they broke 
through the lines at a crucial moment.  The 108th Skeletal Bowmen demolished 
the 147th Legion.  The 240th Bowmen slew the 146th Legion almost to a man.  
The 241st Bowmen scattered the 148th Legion in all directions.  The 109th 
Heavy Cavalry overtook the enemy in their headlong retreat and destroyed the 
145th Legion.
  Bronzeleaf was overrun by Guerin's forces in a hard-fought campaign.  
Guerin's experience improved my skill in Tactics.
  The fall darkened into a frigid early winter.  I failed in my ineffectual 
attempt to cast a Skeletal Army spell.

  Thy humble servant,   Guerin


From: Teleko
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the advent of the spring season, I prepared to quench my thirst for 
adventure.  I directed the 270th Bowmen to remain in the Buccaneer Sea with 
the provincial garrison commander.
  During early summer, I cast a spell giving magical powers of oratory to me.
  Midsummer's night came and went and late summer came.  I rode my flying 
armies into the Amazonian Sea.  Viewing the northwestern horizon, one can 
see a prosperous Sea province known as Kabompo (#804).  It is said that 
Kwoth is the ruler there.  It is known to be occupied by no races.
  Teleko's naval forces took control of the Amazonian Sea practically 
uncontested.  The Amazonian Sea was found to have a tax base of 4 gold.
  With the coming of the fall season, I flew into Kabompo.  To the northeast 
there is a Sea province known as Khurum (#903), an area of no races where 
Kwoth rules.  Northwest of here is Gafsa (#803), a Desert province ruled by 
Kwoth, where Humans dwell.  Their Human warriors prefer to fight in the 
style of Camel Corps.

  A fleet owing their allegiance to Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll 
invaded the province of Kabompo, a Sea area ruled by Kwoth (#3).  Teleko's 
forces conquered Kabompo without any major battles.  Kabompo was found to 
have a tax base of 3 gold.
  With the advent of the early winter season, I flew into Tebessa.

  An army sent by the empire of Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll invaded 
Tebessa, hoping to conquer that province ruled by Kwoth and made up of great 
Deserts.  I was in command of the attacking armies.  The defending forces 
were led by Samantha (#95).  The armies were drawn up into lines of battle 
as shown here:

