  DEFENDING ARMY

  The attackers had the 322nd Eagles and the 326th Dragons in reserve.  I 
marched with my loyal troops, jaws set in grim resolution.  Clarambald (#20) 
led his armies into the fray.  Samantha (#95) stood determinedly at the head 
of her thousands.
  The Skeletal Armies led by Uga-Buga Makumb marched into battle with a 
fanatical fervor.  Teleko's men, ill-supplied in the tortuous desert, 
suffered from thirst.  Samantha's men, ill-supplied in the desert, suffered 
from thirst.  I allowed a prisoner to overhear that allies would soon come 
to augment my forces, then gave him a chance to escape.  The prisoner 
reported the grim news to Samantha, and Samantha deployed her forces with 
too much caution.  Further, Teleko's clever tactical planning assured my 
forces a clear advantage.
  Using my magical powers of Oratory, I started with an inspiring harangue 
to my army, which bolstered their courage.  The Dragons commanded by me were 
not impressed by my lack of leadership ability.
  On the left wing, the Veteran 96th Skeletal Bowmen faced the 292nd Fleet 
Marines.  The 269th Bowmen outflanked the enemy and charged in with full 
strength.  The 321st Eagles soared over the 292nd Fleet Marines and attacked 
them.  The 96th Skeletal Bowmen fought the 292nd Fleet Marines and crushed 
their heads as if they were eggshells.
  On the right flank, the 323rd Trolls were arrayed against the 264th 
Light Cavalry.  The 319th Eagles swooped down on the 264th Light Cavalry and 
attacked them.  The 323rd Trolls fought the 264th Light Cavalry and mowed 
them down like weeds.
  Having found a weak point in the line of the host of Kwoth (#3), a final 
determined thrust finished off their opponent and won the battle for me.  
The 96th Skeletal Bowmen scattered the 292nd Fleet Marines in all 
directions.  The 323rd Trolls annihilated the 264th Light Cavalry.
  Tebessa was overrun by the forces of Teleko.  The battle affected the 
quality of our forces:  the fun head-bashing by the 323rd Trolls in the 
battle has raised the spirits of its warriors, and it has risen to Veteran 
status.  His forces completely destroyed, Clarambald (#20) fled frightened 
and alone to Gafsa.  Her forces completely destroyed, Samantha (#95) escaped 
alone to Limerick.

  Thy humble servant,   Teleko


From: Gridley, Squire to Melantheus
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Winter melted into spring.  Melantheus tried to improve his Sageness, but 
the task was beyond his natural ability.  He discovered nothing in his 
sagely experiments.
  With the coming of the early summer season Melantheus tried to improve his 
Sageness, but the task seemed beyond his aptitude.  He invented nothing in 
his sagely researches.
  With the advent of the late summer season, Melantheus tried to practice 
his Sageness, but the task was beyond his ability.  He invented nothing 
worthy of note in his sagely experiments.
  With the coming of the fall season, Melantheus tried to practice his 
Sageness, but the task seemed beyond his aptitude.  In his sagely 
researches, he discovered a fabulous invention called the Dry Ice Fog!  The 
following benefits are conferred by the Dry Ice Fog:
  Dry Ice Fog reduces the effects of Clairvoyance spells cast on any 
character employed by the Kingdom.  Information obtained will be limited to 
very large-scale activities, while more personal activities will be clouded 
(no more keyhole-peeping!)

  During early winter, Melantheus tried to improve his Sageness, but the 
task was beyond his ability.  He invented nothing valuable in his sagely 
experiments.

  Thy humble servant,   Gridley, Squire to Melantheus


From: Gunga Din, Squire to Tao-Li
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the advent of the spring season, Tao-Li set out to quench his thirst 
for adventure.  He boldly sailed his forces into the Falkland Sea (#1305).
  Windy spring was followed by early summer.  Tao-Li moved into Oceanus 
Cyclopia (#1405) with his Fleet.  Turning to the northeast, one espies a Sea 
area, which is known as Mammoth (#1404).  It is populated by no races and 
no one rules there.  To the east lies a prosperous Sea province called the 
Kilkenny Sea (#1505), populated by Mermen.  It is ruled by no one.  They can 
call on an army of Mermen to defend their province.
  Tao-Li's forces took Oceanus Cyclopia without any major engagements.  
Oceanus Cyclopia was discovered to have a tax base of 1 gold.
  In late summer, Tao-Li attempted an illegal move.  He was ordered to move 
from Oceanus Cyclopia to the Plesiosaurus Sea, further than his navy could 
move.  Instead, he worked hard on his Tactics but was frustrated in his 
self-improvement efforts.
  The summer mellowed into fall.  Tao-Li could not cast a Charm spell 
because Tao-Li had no skill in Psychic Magic.  So, Tao-Li practiced his 
Psychic Magic well but could not improve his Psychic Magic.
  During early winter, Tao-Li could find no soldiers in Oceanus Cyclopia for 
the requested Garrison troops.  So, Tao-Li practiced his Psychic Magic for 
months, but could make no significant progress.

  Thy humble servant,   Gunga Din, Squire to Tao-Li


From: Lallipugh
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season, I set out to quench my thirst for 
glory.  I enlisted enough men in the Dolphin Sea to create the 333rd Bowmen 
and the 334th Bowmen for the army of Odysseus.
  During early summer, I discovered nothing in my sagely experiments.
  Midsummer's day came and went and a hot late summer arrived.  I tried to 
improve my Sageness, but the task was beyond my ability.  In my sagely 
researches, I discovered a fabulous invention called the Strength Elixir!  
The following benefits are conferred by the Strength Elixir:
  The Strength Elixir is a nutritious blend which enables the imbiber to 
maximize the strength gained through exercise.  Its effect is to raise the 
Melee ability of all of the characters of the Kingdom by 1 level.

  In fall, I tried to improve my Sageness, but the task was beyond my 
ability.  I invented nothing worthy of note in my sagely experiments.
  The fall season cooled into early winter.  I discovered nothing in my 
sagely researches.

  Thy humble servant,   Lallipugh


From: Watson, Squire to Amalric
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season, Amalric prepared to quench his 
thirst for glory.  He invented nothing in his sagely researches.
  During early summer, Amalric invented nothing in his sagely experiments.
  Midsummer's day passed and a hot late summer arrived.  Amalric invented 
