  I led a host of loyal soldiers into the battle.  Magnus marched with his 
loyal troops, eyes set in grim resolution.
  The luck of Odysseus's forces was running high for this occasion, for my 
men were in high spirits from a recent successful plundering expedition, and 
I thus enjoyed a significant edge.  As the struggle intensified, the 
tactical wit of Magnus and I appeared evenly matched.

  Across the entire front, the 333rd Bowmen faced the 105th Chariots.  The 
334th Bowmen outflanked the enemy lines and charged in with full force.  The 
333rd Bowmen fought the 105th Chariots and thrust them back.
  The forces of Odysseus broke through and were victorious.  The 333rd 
Bowmen scattered the 105th Chariots in all directions.
  Odysseus's campaign effected the conquest of Kildare.  The battle affected 
the quality of our forces:  the fun head-bashing by the 333rd Bowmen in the 
battle has raised the spirits of its warriors, and it has risen to Veteran 
quality.
  The fall season cooled into early winter.  I spoke to Magnus of the 
greatness of Uga-Buga Makumb's realm and convinced Magnus to pledge his 
allegiance to Uga-Buga Makumb.  After talking to Magnus, I judged him (a Elf 
well known for Psychic Magic) to have an Evil, Berserk character.

  Thy humble servant,   Odysseus


From: Elmer
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season, I prepared to quench my thirst for 
adventure.  I travelled to Falkenheim.  In my travels, I encountered no 
wandering monsters.
  In early summer, I rode into Hollabrand.  In my travels, I saw no 
monsters.
  Midsummer's day passed and a pleasant late summer arrived.  I moved into 
the Ark Royal Sea.  I encountered no wandering monster.
  I heard of a feature in the Icaria Sea (#1007): a Catacombs inhabited by 
the Black Dragon, who holds the Crucible of Elements.
  With the coming of the fall season, Dracona (#38) refused to join with 
Uga-Buga Makumb, citing a long-held family enmity with Uga-Buga Makumb's 
alignment.  After talking to Dracona, I judged him (a Orc famous for 
Necromancy) to have an Evil, Berserk nature.
  During early winter, I cast a Bless spell.  The Dolphin Sea was magically 
blessed and prospered.  The Bless affected no armies in the Dolphin Sea.

  Thy humble servant,   Elmer


From: Presto
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I cast a Phantasmal Armies spell and illusory armies were 
formed for Uga-Buga Makumb.
  With the advent of the early summer season I journeyed to the Buccaneer 
Sea.  During my travels, I was crossing an open field when a Renegade Archer 
spotted me from a distance.  But I spoke to the Renegade Archer with 
respectful words, and a fight was avoided.

  Midsummer's day came and went and late summer arrived.  I moved into the 
Mermaid Sea.  In my travels, I saw no monster.
  During fall, I rode into the Dolphin Sea.  I encountered no monsters.
  With the advent of the early winter season I searched the Altar with the 
intention of overcoming it and whatever guardian lay within it.  I 
encountered the Renegade Necromancer.  I chanted my strange words of magic 
and cast an Invisibility spell, fading into invisibility.  I searched for 
the treasure of the Renegade Necromancer.  Finally I espied a concealed 
chest, and a black tide of greed welled up out of my heart and filled my dry 
throat.  I could see the gleaming treasure which seemed to seductively call 
out to my trembling fingers.  I grabbed the Large Hoard of Gold, my my 
narrow eyes glittering with uncontrolled greed.  I stole 12 gold from 
the Renegade Necromancer.
  I saw nothing special while scouting out the Altar.  I encountered no 
wandering monster.

  Thy humble servant,   Presto


