IMPERIAL OFFICE REPORT

  Into thy heroic dreams cometh an apparition heaven-sent, to speak to thee of
thy progress in thy ambitions for Imperial Office.  It is not for mortal Kings
to know who rivals them for high offices, but the Divine One will allow you to
know thy place in the standings, and how thee compares to thy fiercest foreign
rival for each office (shown under "Riv%" as a percentage: your points divided
by your rival's points, times 100.)

Imperial Office           Best Hope     Rank  Riv%   Second Hope   Rank  Riv%
World Emperor             Uga-Buga Makumb  1   117   None
  An ethereal Emerald Crown appeared on Uga-Buga Makumb's head, and a 
booming voice heard only by Uga-Buga Makumb ordained "This is the Crown of 
the Emperors of the Ancient Dynasty which ruled this world thousands of 
years ago.  It is yours for as long as you are the best hope to become the 
next World Emperor, and can be given to no other.  The Crown will give you 
the ability to know the strength of all your rivals in your quest for 
Empire".  (This information will be shown in your Diplomacy report in future 
gameturns).  Only the tax bases of kings bordering your kingdom that you 
have known for at least one full turn will be shown.

Esteemed High Chancellor  Odysseus         6    66   Amalric          6    66
Imperial Treasurer        Uga-Buga Makumb  1   104   None
  A Golden Abacus mysteriously appeared on Uga-Buga Makumb's desk overnight. 
When Uga-Buga Makumb picked it up to examine it, a silky voice that only 
Uga-Buga Makumb could hear intoned, "This is the Golden Abacus of the 
Treasurers of the Ancient Dynasty which ruled the world millenia ago.  You 
may have its use for as long as your treasury is the world's largest.  The 
Abacus allows you to see the Treasuries of all your rivals in your pursuit 
of wealth (this information will be shown in your Diplomacy report in future 
gameturns).  The Abacus can't be given to another character, and will 
disappear should your hoard ever lose its ranking as the world's richest 
treasury".  Only kings bordering your kingdom that you have known for a full 
turn will be shown.

Imperial Grand Marshal    Guerin           3    75   Teleko           5    68
Imperial Grand Admiral    Guerin           2    45   Uga-Buga Makumb   2    45
Lord High Defender        Odysseus         4     0   Presto           4     0
High Priest Palatine      Guerin           1   121   Teleko           2   100
  As Guerin prayed to his god, an Ivory Rod appeared in between his clasped 
hands, and a divine voice that only Guerin could hear echoed resonantly 
"Because you are the greatest hope to bring the souls of your world to 
deliverance, you may have this Ivory Rod.  The Rod is an artifact which 
belonged to the High Priests Palatine of the Ancient Empire, which many 
years ago succumbed to decadence and petty bickering.  It can be given to no 
other character, and you will have its use as long as you are the greatest 
of Priests.  By its power, you can estimate the moral character of nearby 
Kings, along with nearby heroes whose location you is known to you (the 
accuracy decreases greatly with distance)".  This data will be in your 
Characters report in future gameturns.

Arch-Mage Palatine        Teleko           1   110   Guerin           6    70
  While studying his spells, Teleko looked up to see that an incorporeal 
Platinum Wand had suddenly appeared and was floating in the air in front of 
Teleko.  An enchanting voice spoke from some other dimension, saying "This 
is the Platinum Wand, once used by the Arch-Mages of the Ancient Empire 
which, as you know, collapsed many centuries ago.  It is yours only for as 
long as you are the greatest Mage in the world, and can be given to no other 
character.  The Wand has the power to sense the presence of other magic 
items in the same province: whenever you move into a province, it will tell 
you which magic items are present, but not where they are".

First Elder of Elvenkind  Guerin           1  2200   Teleko           2   700
Angel of Death            Uga-Buga Makumb  1   117   None
  As the Angel of Death, Uga-Buga Makumb has become the most powerful Undead 
King in the world.  His infamy has attracted the service of Circle of 
Wraiths, a greatly feared band of wandering Undead wraiths who have banded 
together in the pursuit of greater power.  When Uga-Buga Makumb is the 
supreme commander at a battle, one non-skeletal unit in the front line, 
chosen at random, will be joined by a flight of screaming Wraiths and become 
fanatical.  Also, the Wraiths will help Uga-Buga Makumb in raising skeletal 
units: when he casts the Skeletal Armies spell, the maximum number of units 
that can be raised by Uga-Buga Makumb increases by 1.

Praetorian Guard          108th Elf Bowmen  1   123   240th Elf Bowmen   2   100
  As the Praetorian Guard, the 108th Skeletal Bowmen has won recognition as 
the land unit most qualified to protect the future World Emperor.  Whenever 
they encamp with other armies, they spend their time telling stories of the 
great battles they have fought.  Their gallantry inspires their fellow 
soldiers to train more intensively, so that when the 108th Skeletal Bowmen 
trains other land units, their chance to improve in quality is doubled, and 
the chance for non-land units is increased by half.


  Note: Kings owning 6% of the world's tax base called for an election.   


