GENERAL INTELLIGENCE REPORT

Kingdom of Babba Sissoko (#0):
  In early winter, Thrym (#59) rode his flying armies over to the Albatross 
Sea.


Kingdom of Kwoth (#3):
  In spring, soldiers bearing the battle-standards of the Kwoth (#3)ian 
empire marched on the Desert province of Chirfa, a land defended by the 
forces of the provincial garrison commander.  Kwoth was in command of the 
invading armies.  The defenders were led by the provincial garrison 
commander.  Chirfa was overrun by Kwoth's men in a bloody campaign.
  In early summer, Ngara was magically flooded.
  In spring, Clarambald (#20) marched on Tebessa (#704) with his command.  
Clarambald found an interesting feature in Tebessa: a Dungeon inhabited by 
the Chimera.
  In spring, Samantha (#95) sailed her command into Kabompo (#804).  
Samantha's naval forces took possession of Kabompo practically uncontested.
  In early summer, Samantha moved into Tebessa (#704) with her Fleet.
  In early winter, Clarambald (#20) led his armies into the fray.  Samantha 
(#95) stood determinedly at the head of her thousands.
  Samantha's men, ill-supplied in the desert, suffered from thirst.
  On the right wing, the Veteran 96th Skeletal Bowmen faced the 292nd Fleet 
Marines.  The 269th Bowmen outflanked the enemy and charged in with full 
strength.  The 321st Eagles soared over the 292nd Fleet Marines and attacked 
them.  The 96th Skeletal Bowmen fought the 292nd Fleet Marines and crushed 
their heads as if they were eggshells.
  On the left flank, the 323rd Trolls were arrayed against the 264th 
Light Cavalry.  The 319th Eagles swooped down on the 264th Light Cavalry and 
attacked them.  The 323rd Trolls fought the 264th Light Cavalry and mowed 
them down like weeds.  His forces completely destroyed, Clarambald (#20) 
fled frightened and alone to Gafsa.  Her forces completely destroyed, 
Samantha (#95) escaped alone to Limerick.

Kingdom of Kahn (#6):
  In fall, magical tornadoes hit the defenders of Bronzeleaf.

Kingdom of Circe (#8):
  In spring, Duqaq (#50) led his navies into the fray.
  The Dwarves commanded by Duqaq were not impressed by his strange 
appearance.
  Across the entire front, the Veteran 316th Bowmen faced the 273rd Fleet 
Marines.  The 293rd Dragons soared over the 273rd Fleet Marines and attacked 
them.  The 316th Bowmen battled with the 273rd Fleet Marines and easily 
destroyed them.  His forces completely destroyed, Duqaq escaped frightened 
and alone to the Flying Fish Sea.


END MOVES REPORT

  Congratulations!  You have attained skill level 5 in Tactics.  At levels 5 
and up, the automatic 20% per level increase in army strength is 
discontinued.  Instead, all characters of this high level gain the following 
Advanced Ability: 
  TACTICAL WARGAME MASTERY:  The chance for a unit to increase in quality 
when Practicing Tactics (or Naval) is increased by 100% (example: an Average 
unit now has a 10% chance to improve per phase).


END MOVES REPORT

  Congratulations!  You have reached skill level 6 in Tactics.  All 
characters of this high level are awarded a new Advanced Ability: 
  TACTICAL MASTERY:  The armies commanded by a character at a battle are 
increased in strength by 15%.


END MOVES REPORT

  Congratulations!  You have attained skill level 5 in Marches.  At levels 5 
and up, the "Ability Level 4" on the March Table is used, and the usual 
increases in army speed on land are not necessarily continued.  Instead, 
your characters of this high level gain the following Advanced Ability: 
  MARCH THROUGH FLOODS:  By using pontoon bridges, ferries and so forth, it 
becomes possible for armies to enter or leave any province affected by the 
Flood spell.  One movement point is deducted from all units which have to 
use this ability, after they have moved.


END MOVES REPORT

  Congratulations!  You have attained skill level 6 in Marches.  Your 
characters of this exalted level are awarded a new Advanced Ability: 
  MARCH CAVALRY:  The character adds one to the movement rate of land armies 
